   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th penile squamous cell carcinoma & AJCC 8th pT1a/pT1b staging",
    "intro": "WHO 5th classifies penile SCC and PeIN into HPV-associated (p16 block-positive) and HPV-independent (p16 negative, often lichen sclerosus / differentiated PeIN / TP53-mutated). In AJCC 8th, lamina propria/dartos invasion is pT1a without high-risk features and auto-upgrades to pT1b if LVI, PNI, or Grade 3 is present.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "HPV stratification & staging pitfalls",
      "points": [
       "HPV-associated SCC (basaloid, warty, warty-basaloid, clear cell, lymphoepithelial): block-type diffuse nuclear and cytoplasmic p16 positivity; arises from basaloid/warty PeIN.",
       "HPV-independent SCC (usual keratinising, verrucous, papillary, pseudohyperplastic, sarcomatoid): p16 negative; frequently associated with lichen sclerosus and differentiated PeIN.",
       "pT1a vs pT1b: presence of LVI, PNI, or any Grade 3 component upgrades lamina propria/dartos invasion from pT1a to pT1b. Corpus spongiosum = pT2; corpus cavernosum = pT3; scrotum/prostate/pubis = pT4."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Squamous Cell Carcinoma of the Penis",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
